          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+space"} complete Segal space
            is a model for the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            regarded as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} internal category in an (∞,1)-category
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              structure
            on the collection of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+sets"} bisimplicial sets
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of all complete Segal spaces, hence for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p We first discuss the model structure
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ForCompleteSegalSpaces"} for complete Segal spaces
          %p as such, and then more generally model structures
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ForCompleteSegalSpaceObjects"} for complete Segal space objects
          %p
            in a suitable ambient model category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} = sSet_{Quillen}
          %h3#ForCompleteSegalSpaces For complete Segal spaces
          %p
            Write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            that is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, sSet]
            for the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+sets"} bisimplicial sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            in particular the
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi Reedy
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, sSet]_{Reedy}
          %p
            which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          %ul
            %li
              projective or injective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model structure on functors
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, sSet]_{inj}
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo →
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c : Set \to sSet
            for the inclusion of sets as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+objects"} discrete objects
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\Delta^{op}, c] : sSet \to [\Delta^{op}, sSet]
          %p for the corresponding inclusion of simplicial sets into bisimplicial sets.
          %p
            When we think in the following of a simplicial set in the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, sSet]
            %em other
            natural such inclusion!).
          #RezkModelStructure.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em model structure for complete Segal spaces
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi Reedy
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, sSet]_{Reedy}
              at the set of morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi a
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W
                    \:=
                    \\{
                    Sp[n] \hookrightarrow \Delta[n]
                    \\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
                    \\cup
                    \\{
                    N(\{a \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} b\}) \to *
                    \\}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the first summand is the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"} spine
              inclusions, while the second summand is the singleton containing the morphism from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              with two objects and precisely one non-identity morphism (and its inverse) from one to the other.
          %p
            This appears originally in section 12 of (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk"}> Rezk
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Equivalently one can replace here the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"} spine
              inclusions with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+Kan+fibration"} inner
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
              inclusions.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [\Delta^{op}, sSet]
              being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
              with respect to the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"} spine
              inclusion says that the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_n \to X_1 \times_{X_0} \cdots \times_{X_0} X_1
            %p
              (with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              factors on the right) is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              of simplicial sets. Therefore the objects which are local with respect to all spine inclusions are precisely the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+spaces"} Segal spaces
            %p
              Accordingly, an object is furthermore local also with respect to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \to *
              if it is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+space"} complete Segal space
          %p The model category structure thus obtained is characterized as follows.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, sSet] = [\Delta^{op}\times \Delta^{op}, Set]
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+sets"} bisimplicial sets
              carries the structure of an
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
              for two bisimplicial sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    hom(X,Y) := i_2^*(Y^X)
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Y
                          %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
                  in the standard
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on presheaves
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 2
                        %mo :
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo →
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_2 : \Delta \to \Delta \times \Delta
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  to the projection
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo →
                        %mi Δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \times \Delta \to \Delta
                  on the second factor, given by
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mn 2
                          %mo :
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ↦
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_2 : [n] \mapsto ([0],[n])
            %p This refines to the structure of a
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"} left proper
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            %p by setting
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  cofibrations are the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              %li
                %p
                  weak equivalences are the
                  = succeed ":." do
                    %strong Rezk weak equivalences
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u : A \to B
                  such that for all
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+space"} complete Segal space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi u
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(u,X) : hom(B,X) \to hom(A,X)
                  is a weak equivalence in the standard
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %p
              The fibrant objects in the structure are precisely the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+spaces"} complete Segal spaces
          %p
            This is essentially (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk"}> Rezk, theorem 7.2
            ). See also (
            %a{:href => "#JoyalTierney"}> Joyal-Tierney, theorem 4.1
            ).
          %h3#ForCompleteSegalSpaceObjects For complete Segal space objects
          %p
            We may generalize from complete Segal spaces to complete Segal space objects in an ambient context other tham
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq (sSet_{Quillen})^\circ
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+combinatorial+model+category"} simplicial combinatorial model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\circ
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
            by it. Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]
            for the
            = succeed "/category" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              There is the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  is is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
                  of the injective
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model structure on functors
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi C
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi inj
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C]_{inj}
              %li
                %p
                  such that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \colon \Delta^{op} \to C
                  are precisely the injectively fibrant objects such that furthermore there image under
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∘
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, C] \to ([\Delta^{op},C])^\circ
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} internal (∞,1)-category
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo ∘
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\circ
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, prop. 1.5.4, remark 1.5.6
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#CartesianMonoidalModelStructure Cartesian monoidal model structure
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, sSet]
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
              = succeed "-structure" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi cSegal
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Delta^{op}, sSet]_{cSegal}
              into a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
          %p
            This is the last clause of (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk"}> Rezk, theorem 7.2
            ). The key lemma for establishing this clause is (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk"}> Rezk, prop. 9.2
            ).
          %h3#relation_to_other_model_structures Relation to other model structures
          %h4#RelQCat Model structure for quasi-categories
          %p
            We discuss the relation to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
          %p
            (See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
            the section
            %em
              %a{:href => "/model+structure+for+dendroidal+complete+Segal+spaces#RelationToDendroidalSets"} Relation to quasi-operads
            \.)
          %p
            A quick way to say the following turns out to be to say that the model structure for complete Segal spaces is the
            %a{:href => "Cisinski+model+structure#SimplicialCompletion"} simplicial completion of Cisinski model structures
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
            (see (
            %a{:href => "#Ara"}> Ara
            )).
          #GroupoidalSimplices.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_J[n] := N(0 \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \cdots \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} n)
                    \\in sSet
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+groupoid"} codiscrete groupoid
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
              objects.) This extends to a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi J
                    %mo :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mi sSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_J : \Delta \to sSet
                    \\,.
          #ComparisonAdjunctions.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              We have the following pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+sets"} bisimplicial sets
            %p The first is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi i
                            %mn 1
                            %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (p_1^* \dashv i_1^*)
                    \:
                    [\Delta^{op}, Set]
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i_1^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{p_1^*}{\to}}
                    [\Delta^{op} \times \Delta^{op}, Set]
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1^*
              sends a bisimplicial set to the simplicial set of its first row
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ,
                        %mo •
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i_1^* : X_{\bullet,\bullet} \mapsto X_{\bullet, 0}
                    \\,.
            %p The other is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mo !
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (t_! \dashv t^!)
                    \:
                    [\Delta^{op} \times \Delta^{op}, Set]
                    \\stackrel{\overset{t^!}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{t_!}{\to}}
                    [\Delta^{op}, Set]
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi t
                          %mo !
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_!
                  assigns the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+simplicial+set"} total simplicial set
                  to a
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+set"} bisimplicial set
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
                  of the functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo :
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo →
                        %mi ssSet
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t : \Delta \times \Delta \to ssSet
                  given by
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi l
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi l
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([k],[l]) \mapsto \Delta[k]\times \Delta_J[l]
                  (with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  from def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidalSimplices"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi t
                          %mo !
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mo ∫
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi l
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo ,
                            %mi l
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi l
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        t_!(X_{\bullet,\bullet})
                        \=
                        \\int^{[k],[l]}
                        X_{k,l} \cdot \Delta[k] \times \Delta_J[l]
                        \\,;
              %li
                %p
                  and where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi t
                          %mo !
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t^!
                  forms in each degree the mapping space
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi t
                          %mo !
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo ↦
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi m
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ↦
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi sSet
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ×
                          %msub
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        t^! : X_\bullet \mapsto
                        \\left(
                        [m,n] \mapsto
                        Hom_{sSet}( \Delta[m] \times \Delta_J[n], X)
                        \\right)
                        \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The composite of the two adjunctions from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComparisonAdjunctions"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mo !
                          %msubsup
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi i
                            %mn 1
                            %mo *
                          %msup
                            %mi t
                            %mo !
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sSet
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i_1^* t^!}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{t_! p_1^*}{\to}}
                    sSet
            %p
              is the identity adjunction: both functors are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
              to the identity functor.
          %p
            This appears at the end of the proof of (
            %a{:href => "#JoyalTierney"}> Joyal-Tierney, theorem 4.12
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              Both adjunctions of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComparisonAdjunctions"}
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
              on simplicial sets and the Rezk model structure for complete Segal spaces on bisimplicial sets, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RezkModelStructure"}
          %p
            This appears (
            %a{:href => "#JoyalTierney"}> Joyal-Tierney, theorem 4.11, 4.12
            ).
          %h4#model_structure_for_dendroidal_complete_segal_spaces Model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operadic
            analog of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+sets"} bisimplicial sets
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
            \/ dendroidal spaces, parameterized over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+category"} tree category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dsSet
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  dsSet := [\Omega^{op}, sSet]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi dSet
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi dsSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \in \Omega \hookrightarrow dSet \hookrightarrow dsSet
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
            with a single edge and no non-trivial vertex.
          %p
            Then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dsSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dsSet
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            is evidently equivalent to that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+sets"} bisimplicial sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ssSet
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi dsSet
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi η
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi dsSet
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ssSet \simeq dsSet_{/\eta}
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  dsSet
                  \\,.
          %p
            By restriction along this inclusion, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
            reproduces the above model structure. See there for more details.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+dendroidal+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for dendroidal complete Segal spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/table+-+models+for+%28infinity%2C1%29-operads"} table - models for (infinity,1)-operads
          %h2#references References
          %p Complete Segal spaces were originally defined in
          %ul
            %li#Rezk
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
              ,
              %em A model for the homotopy theory of homotopy theory
              , Trans. Amer. Math. Soc., 353(3), 973-1007 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/~rezk/rezk-ho-models-final-changes.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#JoyalTierney
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Myles+Tierney"} Myles Tierney
              %em Quasi-categories vs Segal spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0607820"}> arXiv:0607820
              )
          %p A survey of the model structures and their relations is in
          %ul
            %li#Bergner
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julia+Bergner"}> Julia Bergner
              ,
              %em
                A survey of
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty, 1)
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0610239"}> arXiv
              ).
          %p
            The generalization to
            %em complete Segal objects
            in model categories other than
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            was considered in
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,2)
                \-Categories and the Goodwillie calculus
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0905.0462"}> arXiv:0905.0462
              )
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cisinski+model+structures"} Cisinski model structures
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Ara
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dimitri+Ara"}> Dimitri Ara
              ,
              %em Higher quasi-categories vs higher Rezk spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.4354"}> arXiv:1206.4354
              )
          %p
            A model structure for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C2%29-sheaves"} (infinity,2)-sheaves
            of complete Segal spaces is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Meadows"}> Nicholas Meadows
              ,
              %em Local Complete Segal Spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1607.05794"}> arXiv:1607.05794
              )
        .revisedby
